because of your stupid jokes?

536
00:40:09.990 --> 00:40:10.825
I'm sorry

537
00:40:12.451 --> 00:40:13.285
I'm serious.

538
00:40:27.007 --> 00:40:29.635
Do you still write reviews?

539
00:40:30.136 --> 00:40:30.970
What?

540
00:40:31.053 --> 00:40:33.597
Do you still write reviews?

541
00:40:34.098 --> 00:40:35.516
Yes, of course.

542
00:40:36.142 --> 00:40:41.397
You write reviews
for every movie you watch?

543
00:40:41.480 --> 00:40:44.275
No, I watch a lot of movies
and I can't write reviews for all of them.

544
00:40:46.694 --> 00:40:47.945
why do you ask

545
00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:51.740
I thought here.

546
00:40:51.824 --> 00:40:55.327
You try to avoid me.

547
00:40:55.411 --> 00:40:57.496
- This is very annoying.
- Really?

548
00:40:58.289 --> 00:41:01.500
I thought about it too.
We will welcome you at the meeting...

549
00:41:01.584 --> 00:41:03.586
- Your area.
- What?

550
00:41:03.669 --> 00:41:06.755
I will rarely be at home
when we start shooting the movie.

551
00:41:07.256 --> 00:41:10.384
Your area I will leave here.

552
00:41:11.010 --> 00:41:13.262
Hold on, you don't have to…

553
00:41:25.649 --> 00:41:27.985
Nice to meet you. I Song Choo A.

554
00:41:29.195 --> 00:41:30.571
I'm Kim Mubi.

555
00:41:32.072 --> 00:41:35.409
The director really liked Kim
your script.

556
00:41:36.494 --> 00:41:37.536
Thank you.

557
00:41:37.620 --> 00:41:39.038
You are the director.

558
00:41:40.289 --> 00:41:43.292
Probably so. And you are a screenwriter.

559
00:41:45.961 --> 00:41:48.714
What scenario are we talking about?

560
00:41:48.797 --> 00:41:49.632
"Melody".

561
00:41:51.091 --> 00:41:53.302
I'm sorry, but I won't give it to you.

562
00:41:53.385 --> 00:41:55.763
What? But why?

563
00:41:55.846 --> 00:41:58.849
This is my first screenplay.
it has flaws.

564
00:41:59.725 --> 00:42:01.227
Still have to edit.

565
00:42:04.522 --> 00:42:07.024
I have better jobs.

566
00:42:07.107 --> 00:42:08.859
"Love me if you can."

567
00:42:09.527 --> 00:42:11.695
And I'm working on a new script.

568
00:42:11.779 --> 00:42:13.697
But I like this one.

569
00:42:13.781 --> 00:42:15.783
Why mention other works?

570
00:42:16.700 --> 00:42:19.620
I wrote the script
and I don't like him.

571
00:42:21.789 --> 00:42:24.124
Have you picked up other people's ideas?

572
00:42:24.208 --> 00:42:25.292
what did you say

573
00:42:25.793 --> 00:42:27.378
Please. God

574
00:42:27.461 --> 00:42:29.380
A call? Now?

575
00:42:29.463 --> 00:42:30.881
Sorry.

576
00:42:32.675 --> 00:42:35.261
Please don't fight.

577
00:42:41.058 --> 00:42:41.976
A civil servant?

578
00:42:43.102 --> 00:42:46.105
I always wanted to learn Pilates. Damage.

579
00:42:46.981 --> 00:42:48.357
I will say the same about you.

580
00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:51.235
by the way

581
00:42:52.194 --> 00:42:55.030
I knew that I had already heard this story somewhere.

582
00:42:55.114 --> 00:42:57.032
This is your story, right?

583
00:42:58.033 --> 00:42:58.867
No.

584
00:42:58.951 --> 00:43:00.160
Your.

585
00:43:00.244 --> 00:43:02.663
Almost word for word.

586
00:43:03.872 --> 00:43:05.791
And that's why I won't give you the script.

587
00:43:06.417 --> 00:43:09.587
I wrote it out of desperation for a debut.

588
00:43:09.670 --> 00:43:12.089
Check out my other works.

589
00:43:13.007 --> 00:43:14.300
I like this one.

590
00:43:14.383 --> 00:43:17.845
The script is raw and clumsy,
and this is its beauty.

591
00:43:17.928 --> 00:43:19.471
So let it be.

592
00:43:19.555 --> 00:43:21.724
What is the matter? Are you ashamed?

593
00:43:25.144 --> 00:43:27.313
I thought the movie was about me.

594
00:43:27.396 --> 00:43:31.609
I heard that artists are in everything
draw inspiration when in despair.

595
00:43:32.192 --> 00:43:34.695
I will die of shame. This is a definite no.

596
00:43:36.113 --> 00:43:37.323
Don't be shy.

597
00:43:37.990 --> 00:43:41.410
People in this field
always sell their own stories.

598
00:43:45.372 --> 00:43:47.875
Then let me at least edit.

599
00:43:50.419 --> 00:43:52.129
Once I saw a documentary film.

600
00:43:52.212 --> 00:43:55.507
The screenwriter even went
to an ex after a terrible divorce,

601
00:43:55.591 --> 00:43:57.676
to make the film successful.

602
00:43:57.760 --> 00:44:00.095
This is a story about their happy past.

603
00:44:00.971 --> 00:44:02.389
Do you know what movie this is?

604
00:44:07.061 --> 00:44:08.979
This is a classic!

605
00:44:09.647 --> 00:44:10.481
Yes.

606
00:44:11.607 --> 00:44:14.860
Think carefully and make the right decision.

607
00:44:18.280 --> 00:44:20.991
Sorry. Unexpected call.

608
00:44:22.159 --> 00:44:25.579
It was a request for an interview. Do you agree?

609
00:44:25.663 --> 00:44:27.373
Isn't the interview enough?

610
00:44:27.456 --> 00:44:30.376
The iron must be forged while it is hot.

611
00:44:30.876 --> 00:44:33.879
Have you discussed everything?

612
00:44:40.594 --> 00:44:41.428
Ahoy!

613
00:44:43.764 --> 00:44:44.598
Wait!

614
00:44:46.975 --> 00:44:49.561
Are you visiting again?

615
00:44:50.396 --> 00:44:52.356
Yes. And what?

616
00:44:53.273 --> 00:44:54.441
It becomes a habit.

617
00:44:54.525 --> 00:44:56.110
We have such a relationship.

618
00:44:57.277 --> 00:45:00.114
I see, you do know my Mubi.

619
00:45:00.781 --> 00:45:04.159
You said "my Mubi" last time too.

620
00:45:05.077 --> 00:45:06.370
Because she is my girlfriend.

621
00:45:07.454 --> 00:45:08.831
Will you repeat it with her?

622
00:45:10.499 --> 00:45:13.127
I only sometimes call her that.

623
00:45:13.877 --> 00:45:15.921
- I think you are just friends.
- I'm sorry.

624
00:45:16.004 --> 00:45:17.589
And who are you to her?

625
00:45:22.010 --> 00:45:24.096
Don't act like there's something between you.

626
00:45:27.891 --> 00:45:28.892
How to say it?

627
00:45:28.976 --> 00:45:29.852
God

628
00:45:30.894 --> 00:45:32.312
you are funny

629
00:45:32.813 --> 00:45:35.649
Let's pretend we don't know each other and go our separate ways.

630
00:45:36.817 --> 00:45:39.278
Such a one! Did you find it? It can't be!

631
00:45:39.778 --> 00:45:43.532
I put it down to throw it away
but she found her owner.

632
00:45:44.950 --> 00:45:46.785
I knew they were here.

633
00:45:47.703 --> 00:45:51.373
I have a mechanical version of the First Gundam.

634
00:45:51.457 --> 00:45:52.291
Interested?

635
00:45:55.544 --> 00:45:56.378
are you not lying

636
00:46:20.360 --> 00:46:21.695
Greetings!

637
00:46:23.155 --> 00:46:24.573
I'm already leaving.

638
00:46:25.115 --> 00:46:27.117
I will be on time.

639
00:46:27.618 --> 00:46:28.452
OK.

640
00:47:50.033 --> 00:47:51.243
- Congratulations.
- Hello.

641
00:47:51.326 --> 00:47:53.537
The interviewer has just arrived. Coffee?

642
00:47:53.620 --> 00:47:55.038
No, you don't have to.

643
00:47:58.542 --> 00:48:00.127
Sorry for being late.

644
00:48:00.627 --> 00:48:01.879
I'm Kim Mubi…

645
00:48:04.673 --> 00:48:07.009
It is better to get off at the next stop.

646
00:48:15.100 --> 00:48:16.518
My name is Ko Geum.

647
00:48:17.102 --> 00:48:19.354
are you mocking

648
00:48:19.438 --> 00:48:21.690
The magazine often asks for interviews.

649
00:48:22.190 --> 00:48:24.860
I can't refuse.

650
00:48:26.486 --> 00:48:27.321
sit down

651
00:48:28.196 --> 00:48:30.490
Will you go and leave me the office?

652
00:48:42.753 --> 00:48:43.587
are we done

653
00:48:44.671 --> 00:48:46.840
No, there are still a few questions.

654
00:48:46.924 --> 00:48:50.093
show me Are you making them up?

655
00:48:51.178 --> 00:48:52.512
Are these all your questions?

656
00:48:53.931 --> 00:48:55.766
Don't get it wrong.

657
00:48:55.849 --> 00:48:57.851
I ask as much every time.

658
00:48:59.978 --> 00:49:03.982
I won't take it wrong
because there is nothing between us.

659
00:49:05.359 --> 00:49:08.946
I thought the apology worked.

660
00:49:09.029 --> 00:49:13.116
It will not work to apologize in one word.

661
00:49:13.200 --> 00:49:14.368
Learn to apologize.

662
00:49:26.630 --> 00:49:29.216
I don't have much time. I asked my questions.

663
00:49:31.718 --> 00:49:32.552
In that case,

664
00:49:34.012 --> 00:49:36.098
let me ask about you.

665
00:49:36.890 --> 00:49:39.893
- Why is your name Mubi?
- Why do you need to know that?

666
00:49:39.977 --> 00:49:43.355
If the director's name is Mubi,
it makes people curious.

667
00:49:44.231 --> 00:49:47.150
They think:
"She must be very fond of movies."

668
00:49:47.859 --> 00:49:49.027
I hated movies.

669
00:49:50.153 --> 00:49:50.988
Why?

670
00:49:55.659 --> 00:49:58.745
I hated people who loved movies

671
00:49:58.829 --> 00:50:01.581
as if it were something worthy of love.

672
00:50:02.207 --> 00:50:04.751
They are making a fortune out of it,
don't you think so?

673
00:50:04.835 --> 00:50:07.629
As if this is serious art
or the dream of a lifetime.

674
00:50:07.713 --> 00:50:10.257
It's ridiculous to make such a fuss over a movie.

675
00:50:12.676 --> 00:50:15.429
But now you make films yourself.

676
00:50:15.512 --> 00:50:16.847
It's just work.

677
00:50:17.389 --> 00:50:20.892
I want to show that it is possible to make a movie,
without making a fuss.

678
00:50:20.976 --> 00:50:22.102
Who to show?

679
00:50:24.521 --> 00:50:26.857
To the man who gave me that stupid name.

680
00:50:36.199 --> 00:50:38.035
You did not have such a question.

681
00:50:38.118 --> 00:50:40.954
And I think it's time for us to finish.

682
00:50:41.913 --> 00:50:43.498
Do you still hate movies?

683
00:50:43.582 --> 00:50:46.251
I'm too smart
to do what I hate.

684
00:50:47.127 --> 00:50:50.547
Will you watch a movie with me?

685
00:50:53.467 --> 00:50:57.054
As an apology. This is my way of apologizing.

686
00:51:04.144 --> 00:51:06.897
Nice try, but no.

